<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kassite dynasty</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Kassite dynasty ruled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/babylonia">Babylonia</a> for about four centuries after the fall of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/old-babylonian-empire">First Dynasty of Babylon</a>. It was overthrown around 1158 BCE by the Elamite kings <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shutruk-nahhunte">Shutruk-Nahhunte</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kutir-nahhunte">Kutir-Nahhunte</a>, who carried off monuments such as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/code-of-hammurabi">Code of Hammurabi</a> to Susa. This was the military high point of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elamite-confederation">Elamite Confederation</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kassite-dynasty.jpg" alt="Kassite dynasty" width="320" height="281" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: MapMaster · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kassite_Babylonia_EN.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
